00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:38.610
- That's one give, give me a couple more.

00:16:38.610 --> 00:16:40.446
- I mean, like it doesn't
get better than that.

00:16:40.446 --> 00:16:44.233
- I mean, Paul McCartney
and Ringo Star on your song.

00:16:44.233 --> 00:16:47.440
- I mean, they're all pinch me moments,

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:49.890
look getting nominated this
year was a pinch me moment.

00:16:49.890 --> 00:16:50.723
- Right.

00:16:50.723 --> 00:16:52.000
- 'Cause I was not a shoe in,

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:52.833
there was a lot of,

00:16:52.833 --> 00:16:54.539
this was the most
competitive year I ever saw.

00:16:54.539 --> 00:16:55.900
- I totally agree.

00:16:55.900 --> 00:16:59.600
- And so I like just
stayed up all night waiting

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:02.530
and my song was the last one called

00:17:02.530 --> 00:17:04.888
and I had 10 heart attacks before that.

00:17:04.888 --> 00:17:06.160
But you know what?

00:17:06.160 --> 00:17:08.330
It was just the most wonderful moment.

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:10.620
So that was like, yeah.

00:17:10.620 --> 00:17:11.470
- Is that what you normally do?

00:17:11.470 --> 00:17:13.060
Do you normally stay, wait,

00:17:13.060 --> 00:17:13.893
- Yeah.

00:17:13.893 --> 00:17:14.726
- Stay up all night.

00:17:14.726 --> 00:17:15.981
- Yeah, I'm not cool
enough to go to sleep.

00:17:15.981 --> 00:17:18.197
Like all these other
people go yeah, my age

00:17:18.197 --> 00:17:19.230
and my manager.

00:17:19.230 --> 00:17:20.445
Oh yeah.

00:17:20.445 --> 00:17:21.820
- Nah, yeah.

00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:22.814
You're like--

00:17:22.814 --> 00:17:23.647
- You just think you're really cool

00:17:23.647 --> 00:17:24.580
and don't wanna admit it

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:26.290
and I'm not cool and I don't give it,

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:27.830
so I stay up all night

00:17:27.830 --> 00:17:29.507
and admit it and I'm happy to admit it.

00:17:29.507 --> 00:17:32.372
- And then when you hear your
name called, what's that like.

00:17:32.372 --> 00:17:33.647
- It wasn't not my name.

00:17:33.647 --> 00:17:35.066
It was the name of the song.

00:17:35.066 --> 00:17:36.066
And I was just like,

00:17:36.066 --> 00:17:39.815
I just was in shock 'cause
really this was lot,

00:17:39.815 --> 00:17:41.240
this was a smaller movie.

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:42.073
- It is.

00:17:42.073 --> 00:17:44.690
- And I mean, Drew McIntyre's a superstar,

00:17:44.690 --> 00:17:47.210
but there were a lot of, there was like,

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:49.547
there's billion dollar
movies out there with you too

00:17:49.547 --> 00:17:51.385
and Jennifer Hudson

00:17:51.385 --> 00:17:52.720
and a lot of other stars.

00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:53.810
- Oh yeah, the Aretha movie.

00:17:53.810 --> 00:17:55.254
- Yeah.

00:17:55.254 --> 00:17:56.821
- There's a lot of like, it's like,

00:17:56.821 --> 00:17:57.654
a lot of prognosticators,

00:17:57.654 --> 00:17:59.710
most of them did not see
my song in the top five.

00:17:59.710 --> 00:18:00.543
I'm like, yeah.

00:18:00.543 --> 00:18:01.652
- Right.

00:18:01.652 --> 00:18:03.409
- Yeah, see.

00:18:03.409 --> 00:18:04.750
- Right.

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:05.583
Yeah, you're like see, right?

00:18:05.583 --> 00:18:06.780
- I love to prove people wrong.

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:09.075
- You should tell me
about a time then where...

00:18:09.075 --> 00:18:10.545
- That I proved people wrong.

00:18:10.545 --> 00:18:12.038
- All the time.

00:18:12.038 --> 00:18:13.411
Proving people wrong.

00:18:13.411 --> 00:18:15.990
- What are they saying about you?

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:16.823
What are they saying to you?

00:18:16.823 --> 00:18:17.656
- Oh, I don't know.

00:18:17.656 --> 00:18:20.310
Whenever someone says like,
you can't do something.

00:18:20.310 --> 00:18:21.980
I love it, 'cause then I do it.

00:18:21.980 --> 00:18:22.813
- Yeah, you're like, I'm--

00:18:22.813 --> 00:18:24.764
- Soon as they say I can't
do it, I'm gonna do it.

00:18:24.764 --> 00:18:25.597
- You go right at it.

00:18:25.597 --> 00:18:27.070
- Yeah.

00:18:27.070 --> 00:18:27.910
- If you don't want me to do something,

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:29.607
tell me I can't do it.

00:18:29.607 --> 00:18:31.230
(Diane chuckles)

00:18:31.230 --> 00:18:32.130
- All right.

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:35.301
I'm gonna think of one before
this interview is over.

00:18:35.301 --> 00:18:37.387
Who's an artist you
haven't worked with yet

00:18:37.387 --> 00:18:40.323
and you're like one day if possible.

00:18:42.403 --> 00:18:45.010
- Sorry, there's not one
artist to be totally honest.

00:18:45.010 --> 00:18:46.218
- I take any names you can give.

00:18:46.218 --> 00:18:49.870
- But there's people like
the artist I'm supposed work

00:18:49.870 --> 00:18:50.720
with find me

00:18:50.720 --> 00:18:52.047
or I find them somehow.

00:18:52.047 --> 00:18:53.035
- Yeah.

00:18:53.035 --> 00:18:54.494
- So it's not like, well,
if I only work with,

00:18:54.494 --> 00:18:55.520
it's gonna happen.

00:18:55.520 --> 00:18:57.589
I work with really great artists.

00:18:57.589 --> 00:18:59.710
I'm very blessed that way.

00:18:59.710 --> 00:19:00.634
- You've been very blessed like that.

00:19:00.634 --> 00:19:02.009
- Yeah, so.

00:19:02.009 --> 00:19:03.375
- Because you work so often,

00:19:03.375 --> 00:19:06.400
are there artists that
have reached out to you.

00:19:06.400 --> 00:19:08.220
Please don't feel like
you gotta name any names.

00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:09.330
'Cause that's not what I'm asking for,

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:10.550
but what you just say,

00:19:10.550 --> 00:19:11.970
no, I don't think this is a good match

00:19:11.970 --> 00:19:14.310
because I can only imagine
that people reach out to you.

00:19:14.310 --> 00:19:15.337
- Yeah, sure.

00:19:15.337 --> 00:19:17.815
- And what do you base
that on when you say no?

00:19:17.815 --> 00:19:22.100
- I mean honestly like someone
has to have something going

00:19:22.100 --> 00:19:26.310
it's hard to work with
somebody that, starting out.

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:28.842
'Cause it it's so much work, right?

00:19:28.842 --> 00:19:31.619
And so I'd like someone,

00:19:31.619 --> 00:19:33.770
they have to be a great singer

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:35.200
or someone that I think I can help

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:36.840
and that I can fit into their thing.

00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:37.673
- Yeah.

00:19:37.673 --> 00:19:41.410
- Or has something going on
just being totally honest.

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:42.340
- No, but that's so hard.

00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:43.173
- It's so hard.

00:19:44.100 --> 00:19:45.871
- I find it refreshing
that you actually say that

00:19:45.871 --> 00:19:48.550
because on the flip side though,

00:19:48.550 --> 00:19:51.871
because they could use you
almost the like prop themselves.

00:19:51.871 --> 00:19:54.510
- Or sometimes though, if
it depends on the artist,

00:19:54.510 --> 00:19:55.520
it's always artist by artist.

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:56.990
I might hear somebody that I love so much

00:19:56.990 --> 00:19:59.010
that I'm willing to take that chance.

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:00.286
- And you just like, love it.

00:20:00.286 --> 00:20:01.960
Let's let's do this.

00:20:01.960 --> 00:20:02.793
Let's make it happen.

00:20:02.793 --> 00:20:03.640
- Exactly.

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:04.473
- I'm gonna ask you just,

00:20:04.473 --> 00:20:07.883
what was the first album you ever bought?

00:20:07.883 --> 00:20:09.527
- It was a Beatles album.

00:20:09.527 --> 00:20:10.726
"Meet the Beatles".

00:20:10.726 --> 00:20:13.950
- And what was it about them at that time?

00:20:13.950 --> 00:20:15.280
- I just, I was a kid.

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:17.326
I have older sisters just,

00:20:17.326 --> 00:20:19.351
I love them.

00:20:19.351 --> 00:20:23.240
I got to grow up in a time
of really great music.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:24.080
- Yeah.

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:25.689
- So as a songwriter,

00:20:25.689 --> 00:20:29.390
I've always been a sponge
with all kinds of influences.

00:20:29.390 --> 00:20:31.360
That's why I can write
in all these genres.

00:20:31.360 --> 00:20:33.060
- What are some of those influencers,

00:20:33.060 --> 00:20:34.130
you mentioned Motown.

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:35.431
You mentioned the Beatles.

00:20:35.431 --> 00:20:36.443
- Yeah, I got everything.

00:20:36.443 --> 00:20:40.663
I mean every Motown artist,
just soul in general,

00:20:42.425 --> 00:20:44.020
I don't know so much stuff.

00:20:44.020 --> 00:20:45.365
- Just a lot of inspirations.

00:20:45.365 --> 00:20:46.531
- Yeah.

00:20:46.531 --> 00:20:48.160
'Cause when I grew up the
radio played everything.

00:20:48.160 --> 00:20:49.140
- That's true.

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:51.194
What are you listening to these days?

00:20:51.194 --> 00:20:53.350
- I listen to things honestly,

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:55.407
to hear artists I'm working with.

00:20:55.407 --> 00:20:56.640
And to hear what's going on.

00:20:56.640 --> 00:20:58.694
'Cause I have to cause I'm
working with a lot of artists.

00:20:58.694 --> 00:20:59.706
- Right.

00:20:59.706 --> 00:21:00.539
- But I don't like in the daytime,

00:21:00.539 --> 00:21:01.390
I'm doing my own music.

00:21:01.390 --> 00:21:02.830
And when I go home,

00:21:02.830 --> 00:21:04.050
I don't usually listen to music

00:21:04.050 --> 00:21:05.606
'cause my ears need to rest

00:21:05.606 --> 00:21:07.170
and I'm gonna go back the next day.

00:21:07.170 --> 00:21:09.050
- So what are you do when
you're not listening to music?

00:21:09.050 --> 00:21:10.499
'Cause we get inspirations from everyone.

00:21:10.499 --> 00:21:12.727
- I listen to people's conversations.

00:21:12.727 --> 00:21:14.350
I like to go to restaurants

00:21:14.350 --> 00:21:15.740
and listen up to people.

00:21:15.740 --> 00:21:20.740
I read, I watch movies, see friends,

00:21:21.110 --> 00:21:21.943
ideas are everywhere.

00:21:21.943 --> 00:21:23.743
You just have to be open to them.

00:21:23.743 --> 00:21:25.120
- Open to receiving them.

00:21:25.120 --> 00:21:25.953
- Yeah.

00:21:25.953 --> 00:21:27.800
- What haven't you written about yet

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:29.080
that you wanna write about?

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:30.361
What's the story you want to tell?

00:21:30.361 --> 00:21:31.194
- Oh, I don't know.

00:21:31.194 --> 00:21:32.130
- You haven't told about in--

00:21:32.130 --> 00:21:33.916
- I'm not sure what that is.

00:21:33.916 --> 00:21:35.295
I'll let you know.

00:21:35.295 --> 00:21:36.970
And then I'll when I
write it, I'll go see.

00:21:36.970 --> 00:21:39.430
- I you'll be like, that's
one I hadn't done yet.

00:21:39.430 --> 00:21:41.360
Got another one we wanna
take from the audience.

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:42.610
This is from Ibraheem.

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:44.610
How did the idea of the
Cave Session come up

00:21:44.610 --> 00:21:46.510
and working with different artists?

00:21:46.510 --> 00:21:48.080
- Well I was checking out like.

00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:49.429
- If you talk about,

00:21:49.429 --> 00:21:50.262
can you say what the Cave
Session is for those?

00:21:50.262 --> 00:21:54.305
- Yeah, so the cave sessions
is me being DJ Diane.

00:21:54.305 --> 00:21:55.580
It's what, Mark Ronson

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:57.101
or DJ Khaled

00:21:57.101 --> 00:22:00.607
or Calvin Harris does where
they're kind of curating songs

00:22:00.607 --> 00:22:01.643
and artists, right?

00:22:01.643 --> 00:22:04.200
I thought, you know what, I
wanna do the songwriter version

00:22:04.200 --> 00:22:05.050
of that.

00:22:05.050 --> 00:22:07.064
And I write in so many genres,

00:22:07.064 --> 00:22:10.130
you've heard different artists
that I could pull that off,

00:22:10.130 --> 00:22:12.690
And it kind of started

00:22:12.690 --> 00:22:14.457
'cause I have a song that
John Legend I did called

00:22:14.457 --> 00:22:15.320
"Where Is Your Heart?"

00:22:15.320 --> 00:22:16.153
- Yeah.

00:22:16.153 --> 00:22:17.170
- It's on my record.

00:22:17.170 --> 00:22:18.330
I wish I had singles rights,

00:22:18.330 --> 00:22:19.897
'cause it's such a hit.

00:22:19.897 --> 00:22:20.730
- Yeah.

00:22:20.730 --> 00:22:21.790
- Come on, John.

00:22:21.790 --> 00:22:22.623
Gimme singles rights.

00:22:22.623 --> 00:22:24.200
- Yeah, come on John.

00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:25.335
- Come on.
- Let's just make that happen.

00:22:25.335 --> 00:22:28.160
- And he recorded the song.

00:22:28.160 --> 00:22:29.680
He kept saying he was gonna use it.

00:22:29.680 --> 00:22:30.960
He didn't use it.

00:22:30.960 --> 00:22:32.040
I gave it to an artist

00:22:32.040 --> 00:22:34.306
and then he said he wanted it back

00:22:34.306 --> 00:22:35.210
and I piss off an artist

00:22:35.210 --> 00:22:36.774
and then he didn't use it.

00:22:36.774 --> 00:22:37.786
- So how'd that go?

00:22:37.786 --> 00:22:40.284
- Wait, so, then he didn't use it again.

00:22:40.284 --> 00:22:41.257
I gave it to another artist.

00:22:41.257 --> 00:22:42.538
Then he wanted it back again

00:22:42.538 --> 00:22:43.480
and then he didn't use it

00:22:43.480 --> 00:22:45.778
and I go, I believe in this song so much

00:22:45.778 --> 00:22:47.180
with your voice.

00:22:47.180 --> 00:22:49.680
Like it's just one of the
best things I've ever heard.

00:22:49.680 --> 00:22:51.000
If you get a chance to
listen to the album.

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:52.009
- Yeah.

00:22:52.009 --> 00:22:53.022
- Listen to, where is your heart?

00:22:53.022 --> 00:22:54.341
John legend.

00:22:54.341 --> 00:22:55.654
And I finally, I go, you know what,

00:22:55.654 --> 00:22:56.531
and that kind of,

00:22:56.531 --> 00:22:57.900
when I did came up with the
idea of doing my DJ Diane kind

00:22:57.900 --> 00:22:59.290
of thing, I thought,
okay, I'm putting words,

00:22:59.290 --> 00:23:00.560
where is your heart on here.

00:23:00.560 --> 00:23:01.610
It needs to be heard.

00:23:02.810 --> 00:23:03.690
- This is from Lauren.

00:23:03.690 --> 00:23:04.800
What's up Lauren.

00:23:04.800 --> 00:23:06.293
- What songs do you.

00:23:06.293 --> 00:23:09.453
- What songs do you have on repeat?

00:23:10.300 --> 00:23:12.240
- I mean, nothing really?

00:23:12.240 --> 00:23:13.890
I mean, I'm just I'm well, okay.

00:23:13.890 --> 00:23:16.340
To be honest, when I'm writing,
I'm repeating all day long,

00:23:16.340 --> 00:23:17.919
I'm playing over and over.

00:23:17.919 --> 00:23:20.330
So I'm kind of my stuff's on repeat,

00:23:20.330 --> 00:23:22.180
but it's like when I was a kid,

00:23:22.180 --> 00:23:23.586
my dad got a shed in the backyard.

00:23:23.586 --> 00:23:26.670
My parents couldn't listen
to me playing my songs over.

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:27.570
- Oh, they put you in a shed.

00:23:27.570 --> 00:23:28.403
- Yeah, they did.

00:23:28.403 --> 00:23:29.790
They go, it's like, okay,

00:23:29.790 --> 00:23:31.500
work on those songs outside in the winter,

00:23:31.500 --> 00:23:33.280
there'd be a little heater there.

00:23:33.280 --> 00:23:34.230
So yeah.

00:23:34.230 --> 00:23:36.600
That's what I'm, that's what's on repeat.

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:38.796
I'm always just trying to
figure stuff out as I'm doing.

00:23:38.796 --> 00:23:40.846
- And you just know it when you feel it.

00:23:40.846 --> 00:23:41.679
- Yeah.

00:23:41.679 --> 00:23:42.950
And then you go on to the
next part of you're like,

00:23:42.950 --> 00:23:44.064
okay, I got that figured out.

00:23:44.064 --> 00:23:45.020
- Yep.

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:46.180
- Onto the next piece.

00:23:46.180 --> 00:23:48.360
And then you just piece
it together bit by bit.

00:23:48.360 --> 00:23:49.522
- Yeah.

00:23:49.522 --> 00:23:50.854
- I love that approach to it.

00:23:50.854 --> 00:23:53.560
- It's being a craftsman.

00:23:53.560 --> 00:23:55.852
It's funny, I was with some of
my music friends last night,

00:23:55.852 --> 00:23:57.810
we were talking about that
you could be an artist

00:23:57.810 --> 00:23:58.770
or a craftsman

00:23:58.770 --> 00:23:59.603
and I go, no.

00:23:59.603 --> 00:24:00.621
- Talk about the difference.

00:24:00.621 --> 00:24:01.454
What's the difference?

00:24:01.454 --> 00:24:03.179
- No, you're both
because you can't be one.

00:24:03.179 --> 00:24:07.273
You can't be a great artist
without being a great craftsman.

00:24:07.273 --> 00:24:08.260
- Right.

00:24:08.260 --> 00:24:09.266
- And care about craftsmanship.

00:24:09.266 --> 00:24:10.700
- Yeah, because it's a craft.

00:24:10.700 --> 00:24:13.270
So yeah, that was it's interesting.

00:24:13.270 --> 00:24:14.837
When we were talking a
conversation last night.

00:24:14.837 --> 00:24:17.970
- Do you see any changes
besides the million

00:24:17.970 --> 00:24:19.810
and one songwriters on every song?

00:24:19.810 --> 00:24:20.960
- Songwriting by committee?

00:24:20.960 --> 00:24:22.003
- Yeah, like, do you see--

00:24:22.003 --> 00:24:23.282
- I hate committees.

00:24:23.282 --> 00:24:24.528
- I was gonna, essentially
that's (indistinct)

00:24:24.528 --> 00:24:25.648
committees that's.

00:24:25.648 --> 00:24:27.710
- I came up with that word.

00:24:27.710 --> 00:24:28.543
- That's good.

00:24:28.543 --> 00:24:29.660
- Not that the songwriters are committees,

00:24:29.660 --> 00:24:31.644
but just committees in
general are committees.

00:24:31.644 --> 00:24:35.014
- And talk to me about
what you don't like about

00:24:35.014 --> 00:24:35.847
that process.

00:24:35.847 --> 00:24:38.570
It's about the passion of
one person, not a committee.

00:24:38.570 --> 00:24:40.632
The committee is, what do you think?

00:24:40.632 --> 00:24:41.465
What do you think?

00:24:41.465 --> 00:24:42.700
What do you, so what do you.

00:24:42.700 --> 00:24:44.420
No, it's what do you feel?

00:24:44.420 --> 00:24:45.569
And what is one person?

00:24:45.569 --> 00:24:47.520
That's how things get done.

00:24:47.520 --> 00:24:48.470
It's by passion.

00:24:48.470 --> 00:24:50.735
- I think that also takes a
certain amount of confidence.

00:24:50.735 --> 00:24:51.797
- Yeah.

00:24:51.797 --> 00:24:54.240
- In what you're, what
you're putting down.

00:24:54.240 --> 00:24:57.134
- I haven't had a problem with
self confidence in my work.

00:24:57.134 --> 00:24:58.447
